## Review-package anchors

9ef1b6ccb872494148c8b7445d02137d12729c2344b845450176cef4a4400fb6  SHA256SUMS.txt (review package, 22 files)
671c07147e42233aedadbfcd22547ac6e10ec3fd193efaae7ea955eed6c3af4e  SHA256SUMS_digicert.tsr (RFC 3161 timestamp over SHA256SUMS.txt)

The RFC 3161 token above was issued by DigiCert (http://timestamp.digicert.com). Its
`messageImprint` digest equals the `SHA256SUMS.txt` hash on the line above, so the
timestamp covers exactly that file. The review package itself is not published; its
manifest hash is anchored here so that a later release of it can be checked against this commit.

A second timestamp from FreeTSA was attempted on the same manifest and **failed**: the
service returned a 50-byte error record (`Bad request format or system error`), not a
token, both on the original request and on a re-submission of the identical `.tsq`.
`SHA256SUMS_freetsa.tsr` is that error record and must not be read as a timestamp.
Only the DigiCert token is evidence; a second independent TSA remains outstanding.

Note on status: item 1 is a correction posted after two earlier messages of mine did
not reach the list; item 5 is a draft I have deliberately not submitted.

## Revision note — why two values above changed

This anchor was first published with `f87e2c85…` for item 5 and `33d462ab…` for the
review-package manifest. Both were correct when written and are no longer the current
bytes, so the anchor was corrected rather than left standing as a false claim:

- **item 5** (`14_稿件5_巴黎投稿AB_20261117.md`): edited after the anchor was written,
  during the S1–S10 review pass. Old `f87e2c85cfc97ecf91e5fc8cc74cb7e4b70de13c6c651a9c4a8a11af7e69768c`,
  new `dac18ed797314d1b53f5e8d17b14ef93e6d6126607a491b013637783cf357e3b`. The draft is held, never sent,
  so no recipient is affected.
- **review package** (`SHA256SUMS.txt`): regenerated after the final review edits and then
  time-stamped. Old `33d462ab175f2730aa1fb4acaf30903cbd029824e1ff4ff4bf9e2df598809b79`,
  new `9ef1b6ccb872494148c8b7445d02137d12729c2344b845450176cef4a4400fb6`. The DigiCert token was
  re-issued over the new manifest (see the `.tsr` hash above).
- The four already-sent items are unchanged: their hashes still match the text that went out.

